+## Targeted diagnostic testing
+
+Use the controller's supplied validation results for the exact bound candidate as the full-suite execution evidence. Do not rerun the full test suite or a configured full-suite validation command as the Reviewer. The controller still owns and must execute every required baseline, candidate, and final check; this policy does not remove any required check or coordinator integration validation.
+
+Additional test execution is optional and must be permitted by your existing role permissions. Run it only to resolve a concrete review uncertainty. Prefer the smallest meaningful set of existing tests, or a small permitted reproduction using existing fixtures, that might be affected by the Writer's changes, considering the changed behavior, callers, dependencies, shared helpers and fixtures, and relevant failure or regression paths. Do not limit selection to changed test files. For repair reviews, focus additional execution on the current repair and relevant unresolved findings; do not routinely repeat unaffected tests.
+
+Before an additional diagnostic run, briefly identify the uncertainty and why the selected tests address it. Use established repository test entry points and preserve source-origin and environment requirements. Do not edit candidate files, change permissions, alter fixtures, or relax assertions to make a run succeed. If the affected scope is broad or targeted execution cannot establish adequate evidence, inspect the supplied full-check evidence and use the normal repair/stop outcome for missing verification rather than running the whole suite yourself.
+
+Report the exact selected tests/commands, actual outcomes, and execution limitations in notes or finding evidence. These observations are advisory: they do not create validation IDs, change the frozen validation profile, or substitute for controller-owned checks. Use only current-candidate bound results; prior-source results and cached passes are not proof for changed source. If no additional tests were run, state that assessment used the supplied validation evidence and source inspection.
+
+This limits duplicate execution, not review coverage. Continue assessing every applicable criterion, regression risk, and the complete required review scope, including the full base-to-source diff at final review. Never accept missing, failed, stale, skipped-only, or otherwise inadequate required evidence.
+
